345: ## S4. The other source sectors are already coefficient-generic
346: 
347: The ordinary III, IV and II root proofs F42--43 were
348: written with the full holomorphic unit coefficients:
349: \[
350:  \begin{array}{ll}
351:  III:&y^2=x^3+q\,a(q)x+q^2b(q),\quad a(0)\ne0,\\
352:  IV:&y^2=x^3+q^2a(q)x+q^2b(q),\quad b(0)\ne0,\\
353:  II:&y^2=x^3+q\,a(q)x+q\,b(q),\quad b(0)\ne0 .
354:  \end{array}
355:  \tag{S51.14}
356: \]
357: The displayed root substitutions, finite-deck characters,
358: blowup centres, quotient maps and contractions in those
359: proofs use precisely these equations. The marked generator's
360: central point is fixed by the original component map:
361: nonidentity for III/IV and identity for II. Finite
362: linearization retaining the marked sections is the
363: explicit averaging map in S3. The good-III and good-IV
364: Cartier differences \(E_P-E_O\), and the cancellation
365: at the six-point good-II correspondence, are therefore
366: unchanged as actual divisor identities. Higher section
367: contact changes the finite point on the exceptional
368: curve, but every contracted centre is the recorded
369: infinity point, so the identities remain valid.
370: 
371: For the \(I_1^*\) sources the F36/F38/F49 proof is also
372: coefficient-generic. On the actual minimal quadratic
373: Tate root it retains
374: \[
375:  q_T=z^2u(z^2),\qquad Z_G=zv(z),\qquad
376:                   v(z)v(-z)=-u(z^2).
377:  \tag{S51.15}
378: \]
379: Here \(u,v\) are arbitrary nonvanishing holomorphic units.
380: The first equality follows from the analytic inverse
381: of the Tate \(j\)-series and the even source base; the
382: second is the marked odd component; the last is the
383: literal deck equation \(Z_G(-z)=q_T/Z_G(z)\).
384: Thus the source norm, root Picard character, four-point
385: blowup quotient and the equality
386: \(\beta^*N=\pi^*\mathcal M+E_0+E_1\) all retain arbitrary
387: source coefficients. The translation exchanging the
388: two indicated exceptional curves is the actual \(Q\)
389: translation, not a representative-model identification.
390: F49 then gives the exact affine and line conjugacies,
391: with the annular map and any moved blowup centres
392: transported as specified there.
393: 
394: At the selected whole-zero \(I_1\), the actual Tate
395: period and Picard characters are arbitrary nonzero
396: holomorphic units. The only vanishing scalar is its
397: specified simple base factor. K26--30 already retain
398: these units, their logarithms, the exact cusp-origin
399: difference and its bounded Cox extension. Thus their
400: cusp, page and normal-frame comparisons do not impose
401: a hidden special-source coefficient.
